The original verity is located here
-----------------------------------
repo:   git@git1.corp.cat.com:/cat/ess-csf/web_manager-a
tag:    CoreTelematics_2020.17.1
commit: 9a4cc7d590e76fd5b43a8ce376f0302aad317c82
files:
    .\web_manager-a\tgt_gcc_5.1.0_a6n2\ServiceDashboard_Lite_A6N2_02020082802.verity
    .\web_manager-a\tgt_gcc_5.1.0_a6n2\ServiceDashboard_Lite_A6N2_02020082802.verity_verify


Mounting the verity
-----------------------------------
mkdir -p "${mountDir}" "${tmpDir}"
sudo mount -o loop,ro,user "${verityImage}" "${mountDir}"
sudo rsync -rlW --delete --inplace "${mountDir}/." "${tmpDir}/."
sudo chown -R $USER: "${tmpDir}/."
sudo umount "${mountDir}"
rm -rf "${mountDir}"

Now ${tmpDir} contains the original contents of the mounted verity.

Creating the patch
-----------------------------------
The build process applies the patch that is created with the following:

diff -ruN ServiceDashboard ServiceDashboardNew > ServiceDashboard.patch

Where the "ServiceDashboardNew" is the edited version of the contents, and
"ServiceDashboard" is the original version of the contents that came from
the verity.

The patch is then applied with:

patch -u -p0 < ServiceDashboard.patch
